WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:12.400
[Penicillin and Venereal Disease]

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:25.600
[Presented by the U. S. Public Health Service in cooperation with State and Local Health Departments]

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:30.840
[This is a portion of the motion picture Penicillin
in Medicine and Surgery produced by 

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:40.780
Grant, Flory &amp; Williams and distributed by E. R. Squibb &amp; Sons]

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:46.800
[ Narrator: ] The United States Public Health
Service has had a major role in determining

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:52.260
the value of penicillin in the treatment of
venereal disease. Much of this work has been

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:55.840
done under the direction of Dr. J.R. Heller,
Jr.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:01.570
[ Dr. J.R. Heller: ] More than 200,000 new
infections of syphilis are acquired in this

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:07.570
country each year. All are actually or potentially
highly infectious.

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:11.610
If these patients could be found and treated
before they have a chance to spread their

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:16.350
infections, there would soon be a marked reduction of syphilis.

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:22.880
Increased alertness and diagnosis is important
as a first step in bringing this about.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:28.460
Early diagnosis not only aids in reducing syphilis,
but also is important in improving the

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:32.200
outlook for cure of the individual patient.

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:39.200
[ Narrator: ] One or more of these cases, too
often unnoticed or unlooked for, may be present

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:45.369
in the physician's waiting room. Physicians
should examine the genitalia, the skin, and

00:01:45.369 --> 00:01:49.090
the mucosa for lesions of early syphilis.

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:55.799
They should employ both darkfield microscopic
examinations and blood serologic tests. Look

00:01:55.799 --> 00:02:09.219
for such symptoms as early penile lesions,
the lip chancre, and the noticeable gumma.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:22.150
Other manifestations are the sore throat,
any mucosa lesions which do not heal in ten

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:29.680
days, any unexplained loss of hair...

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:36.900
general malaise, loss of weight, fever, or
macular and maculopapular and group follicular eruptions.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:48.520
The clinician may occasionally be surprised
to find among his patients long-neglected

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:55.310
cases. such as this example of advanced syphilis.

00:02:55.310 --> 00:03:01.450
The early latent stage often passes unrecognized.
There are probably scores of latent syphilis

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:05.069
cases passing through your office each year.

00:03:05.069 --> 00:03:09.819
Blood and spinal fluid tests are the principle
diagnostic procedures available in the early

00:03:09.819 --> 00:03:12.650
latent stage of syphilis.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:17.599
This applies also to the late latent stage
with an increased probability of positive

00:03:17.599 --> 00:03:24.599
spinal fluid findings. For example, the colloidal
gold test for paresis appears in this manner.

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:34.560
And is usually indicated by this type of curve.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:37.280
[Chart reading Spinal Fluid Dilutions in .4% Sodium Chloride Controls is shown,]

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:44.140
While the test for a [?] reaction responds
in this manner.

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:49.640
Let us look at some typical latent manifestations
of syphilis.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:56.520
Penile lesion

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:01.920
Aneurysm.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:09.090
Charcot's joint.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:22.540
Ocular nerve palsy and optic atrophy.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:26.619
Syphilis of the central nervous system.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:32.640
Paresis or tabes.

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:38.540
On the basis of present evidence, penicillin
appears to have great value in the treatment

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:42.300
of syphilis in virtually all stages and manifestations.

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:49.300
This lesion, which we saw earlier, has been
treated with penicillin. Treatment was on

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:54.420
a schedule of forty thousand units every three hours, which will total 

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:57.520
two million four hundred thousand units in seven and one half days.

00:04:59.379 --> 00:05:03.879
The healing of this lesion was accompanied
by a serologic reversal which occurred

00:05:03.879 --> 00:05:10.879
over a five-week period. We cannot always expect
such ideal results, however.

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:18.980
The more obstinate cases may require prolonged therapy and attention. 

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:27.140
Serologic reversal may require many weeks or months, and in some
rare cases, even clinical symptoms may recur.

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:34.869
No final statement can be made at this time
regarding the place penicillin will eventually

00:05:34.869 --> 00:05:37.710
occupy in the treatment of syphilis.

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:41.089
Developments are occurring are so rapidly
that it is not feasible to recommend here

00:05:41.089 --> 00:05:46.969
precise dosages and methods of administration,
but it is important to keep abreast of progress

00:05:46.969 --> 00:05:48.399
in the field.

00:05:48.399 --> 00:05:52.729
Your professional societies and journals,
your health departments, and the United States

00:05:52.729 --> 00:05:59.729
Public Health Service are all reliable sources
of information.

00:05:59.789 --> 00:06:05.539
Against gonorrhea, the advent of penicillin
presents a strong and efficient weapon. Here

00:06:05.539 --> 00:06:11.360
we can be more definite in our suggestions.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:17.659
Under penicillin therapy, the gonorrhea patient
is completely ambulatory. 

00:06:17.659 --> 00:06:22.990
Toxic reactions are almost unknown. Discomfort and pain are slight.

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:28.339
Fortunately the gonococcus is highly susceptible
to penicillin, and control is apparent almost

00:06:28.339 --> 00:06:30.619
at once.

00:06:30.619 --> 00:06:36.279
The patient from whom this specimen was taken
received four intramuscular doses of 50,000

00:06:36.279 --> 00:06:43.279
units of penicillin in aqueous solution at
three-hour intervals. Total:  200,000 units.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:52.920
Within 24 hours, the smear should be negative.
Complications such as epididymitis, arthritis,

00:06:53.059 --> 00:06:57.619
and endocarditis require larger and prolonged
dosage.

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:05.620
As an alternative procedure, a single dose
of 300,000 units of penicillin in oil and

00:07:05.789 --> 00:07:11.909
wax has proved effective in gonorrhea with
a minimum of inconvenience to the patient.

00:07:11.909 --> 00:07:18.909
[Warning: The maximum penicillin dosage for gonorrhea may inhibit the normal development

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:23.839
of clinical and serologic symptoms of a concomitant
syphilis infection.]

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:31.640
[A blood specimen for serologic testing should
be taken before therapy is begun.]

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:37.419
[Each gonorrhea patient should be strongly
urged to report for serologic and other tests

00:07:37.419 --> 00:07:43.579
for syphilis at suitable intervals for three to
six months after completing the treatment for gonorrhea.]

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:50.420
[ Dr. John R. Heller, Jr.: ] Whatever the
future may hold for penicillin therapy, we

00:07:50.569 --> 00:07:56.349
physicians already have in our hands weapons,
which with proper medical usage should enable

00:07:56.349 --> 00:08:01.009
us to reduce materially the amount of venereal
disease in the United States.

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:13.360
[The End]

